      "card_ids": ["C12"],
      "claim": "In healthy men, 11C-SCH23390 showed rapid transfer into the brain with 1.2% of injected radioactivity present in the brain at 4.5 minutes, providing direct human evidence of meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The closest structural analogue and multiple additional related compounds show direct in vivo BBB penetration across rodents, non-human primates, and humans. The single negative analogue is less similar and is outweighed by consistent positive CNS-access evidence.",
